1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,120
Every day, the rules behind our digital
lives can change,

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,240
a clause, a permission, a new use of your
data.

3
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,120
The question is simple.

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:12,240
What changed and where is the proof?

5
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:17,690
PolicyWatcher helps people and
organisations follow

6
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:20,150
changes in the policies of digital
services.

7
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:23,690
Explore the source, compare versions and
understand

8
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:25,650
why a change deserves attention.

9
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:28,690
Clear information with a path back to the
evidence.

10
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:36,170
Today, PolicyWatcher has two complementary
sides.

11
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:39,210
The stable service supports everyday use.

12
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,810
Engine 6 Preview is a separate, private
workspace for

13
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:44,170
testing the next generation.

14
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:47,890
One mission, with a clear boundary between
public operation

15
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:49,370
and experimental results.

16
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:54,430
The new pipeline starts before artificial
intelligence.

17
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,470
Source contracts check document identity,
language,

18
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:01,170
required sections and the ending of the
policy.

19
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:03,890
A successful download is only the
beginning.

20
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:07,490
Incomplete or ambiguous material is held
for review.

21
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:13,330
Each capture becomes a traceable artifact.

22
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,570
Versions can be compared against preserved
evidence.

23
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:20,090
A candidate change requires two fresh
observations at

24
00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:21,350
least an hour apart.

25
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:25,290
A retry or a cached response does not
become a second confirmation.

26
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:33,770
Analysis must point to exact passages
before and after the change.

27
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:36,270
A separate verifier checks the evidence.

28
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:40,010
High impact or uncertain cases move to
human review.

29
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:43,090
In the hosted Preview, automatic public
changes and

30
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:44,650
notifications remain disabled.

31
00:01:49,750 --> 00:01:54,010
Behind the interface, durable jobs connect
runs, tasks,

32
00:01:54,230 --> 00:01:55,790
attempts, and stored artifacts.

33
00:01:56,610 --> 00:01:57,970
Checkpoints support recovery.

34
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:01,310
Preview and compare make the work
inspectable, including

35
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:04,750
a comparison of two extractors on the very
same captured response.

36
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:10,310
Research does not stop at a new build.

37
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:14,130
Local tests, hosted checks, source
completeness and

38
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:16,990
observations over time answer different
questions.

39
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:20,230
500 policies a day is the scale target.

40
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:23,410
Full qualification at that scale is still
in progress.

41
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:30,830
The Public Research Diary opens the
architecture, decision

42
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:32,770
flow, and entity relationships.

43
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:36,250
GitHub records the implementation and its
limits.

44
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:38,610
This is continuous engineering.

45
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:41,930
Measure, challenge, refine, and show the
work.

46
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,140
Explore PolicyWatcher today.

47
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,320
Inspect Engine 6 Preview.

48
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,780
Follow the research, because understanding
a policy change

49
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:54,900
should begin with evidence and lead to a
clearer decision.
